<title>POLAND: Polish broad money up 2.8 pct in July 1-10 - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money up 2.8 pct in July 1-10 - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 4.23 billion zlotys, or 2.8 percent, in July 1-10 to 155.39 billion after a 2.0 pct rise in all of June, preliminary central bank figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Broad money grew 14.5 percent since the start of the year.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		   JULY 1-10    JUNE    JULY '96</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)	     2.8	  2.0	 2.3</p>
<p>  Money in bln			   155.39     151.16    119.58</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)     26.80	26.39     21.97</p>
<p>  National currency		    128.59     124.77     97.62</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		   28.07	26.84     22.49</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector   95.59	94.31     65.16</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
